# Summary of Sex Determination in Fruit Flies

@left

![Slide image 4](assets/lect06e-x_linked_genes_2/image_004.png)

@right

- [*metafemale*]{color=red underline=true} (or superfemale) is a low viability Drosophila with a female phenotype [(X\:A ratio > 1)]{color=red}
- [*metamale*]{color=blue underline=true} (or supermale) is a low viability Drosophila with a male phenotype [(X\:A ratio < ½)]{color=blue}
- [*intersex*]{color=purple underline=true}: intermediate sexual development in this fruit-fly X:A model (½ < X\:A ratio < 1)


